job.plain_text_description:
We govern the beautiful game and ensure it's run with transparency and integrity.
Join our team in Miami and support us on our mission.

These are your key tasks:

- Conducting autonomously ethics proceedings in accordance with the FIFA Code of Ethics;
- Investigating ethics proceedings, including the review and analysis of financial records, the use of forensic audit techniques, and the development of financial investigative strategies;
- Drafting communications and request for information to the interested/accused parties within an ethics proceeding;
- Supporting the preparation of witness interviews and witness statements, and, when necessary, coordinating such tasks with other departments or external experts within the context of ethics proceedings;
- Liaising with FIFA departments and subject-matter experts to secure support for FIFA Ethics Committee matters;
- Supporting the relevant chairperson and members of the Ethics Committee by preparing case files, legal analyses, and draft decisions to facilitate effective deliberations;
- Assisting the relevant chairperson of the FIFA Ethics Committee in the preparation of meetings;
- Assessment of legal aid requests, witness protection, witness/victim’s psychological support, and when necessary, coordinating such tasks with other departments or external experts within the ethics proceedings;
- Drafting final Reports within an ethics proceeding;
- Analyzing testimonials and other documentary evidence, including financial and audit records, to weigh its credibility and probative value within the context and standards of the FIFA Code of Ethics;
- Conduct legal analysis of FIFA precedent and CAS jurisprudence to support the drafting of final investigation reports and Ethics Committee decisions;
- Drafting decisions of the Adjudicatory Chamber;
- Contributing to the ongoing development of workflows, templates, and best practices to ensure efficiency and consistency;
- Identify and recommend measures to prevent violations of the FIFA Code of Ethics and promote the safeguarding and integrity of football worldwide;
- Close collaboration and support to the Head of Department in creating efficient ethics proceedings (i.e. determining processes, workflow, template creation, etc.);
- Ensuring a worldwide recognition of the activity of the Investigation Department and the Judicial Bodies Subdivision;
- Assistance in preparing any report related to the activities of the ethics department, including newsletters, status reports, etc.
- Holding and participating in workshops with FIFA employees, member associations or confederations on Judicial Bodies-related issues.

We work hard at FIFA.
We are dedicated, ambitious and innovative.

And we respect our values. Always.

For all roles, we seek talented people with an entrepreneurial spirit and a global mindset.

The specific competencies we require for this position are:

- Excellent legal drafting and presentation skills in English;
- Proficiency legal drafting in Spanish or French is an asset;
- Good knowledge of football governance as well as of FIFA’s regulations, and proven experience in FIFA’s Disciplinary and Ethics proceedings;
- Ability to conduct analysis and draw out conclusions;
- Strong ability to analyze financial data, audit findings, and forensic accounting reports to detect and understand irregularities;
- Excellent editorial skills;
- Good planning and organisational skills;
- Solid IT-know how;
- Ability to work unsupervised and precisely;
- Ability to work well under pressure and to respect deadlines;
- Good analytical skills;
- Conscientiousness, accuracy and quality;
- Punctuality;
- Proactive approach;
- Rigorous and consistent, particularly when handling large amounts of documents;
- Team player with good interpersonal relations;
- Excellent communication skills;
- Cooperative and team-oriented mindset, fostering transparent communication and knowledge sharing;
- Motivated, autodidact, dynamic and proactive personality;
- Ability to adapt to changing priorities;
- Agility;
- Ability to adapt to an international and multicultural environment;
- Pleasant and empathetic;
- Law University degree (Bar Exam);
- Post-Graduate in Sport law is an asset;
- Training or certification in white-collar investigations (including forensic accounting, CPA, CFE, etc.) or prior experience in an audit firm is an asset;
- Minimum 6-8 years of experience in similar positions, dealing with disciplinary and ethics regulations matters in a sports governing body;
- Experience handling cases of misappropriation of funds, bribery and corruption, and working alongside compliance, finance teams, or external auditors, is a strong asset;
- Native/C2 in English;
- Proficiency in any other FIFA language (F / ES) is an asset;
- Proficient in Word / PowerPoint / Excel/Jira;
- Ability to leverage AI tools to enhance investigative efficiency while ensuring accuracy, confidentiality, and compliance with applicable legal and ethical standards.

The biggest benefit of a career at FIFA is the privilege to work for the beautiful game and create something that matters.

Alongside that privilege, we also offer some extra perks and benefits:

Health insurance: We offer generous medical, vision, and dental insurance coverage.

Continuous learning: We care about your development and encourage internal mobility, offering a variety of training and education to help achieve it.

Retirement: We offer generous 401(k) employer contributions.

Vacation: Maintain a healthy work/life balance with a generous vacation allowance.

FIFA has established a Local FIFA Subsidiary in Brazil to work together with FIFA Zurich to deliver the biggest women’s sporting event in the world, the FIFA Women’s World Cup 2027™ (“FWWC2027”) that for the first time ever, is hosted in South America in Brazil. Now is your time to be part of the workforce that is creating this unique and unforgettable experience.

Please submit your CV in English, as it will be reviewed by an international team.

Sitting within the Ticketing & Hospitality Department, Hospitality (along with Ticketing) aims to deliver the most engaging and innovative FIFA Women's World Cup 2027™ experience for all commercial partners, customers, guests and the FIFA football family.

Reporting organizationally to the Head of FWWC27 Hospitality Operations, the Hospitality Operations & Infrastructure Venue Manager will help serve Hospitality efforts for the FIFA Women’s World Cup 2027™ that is hosting 32 teams across 8 venues.

This role will be responsible for the supervision of the implementation of all stadium Hospitality infrastructure requirements and technical operations across all stadiums of the FIFA Women’s World Cup 2027™, and later assuming a fixed position as Rio de Janeiro Stadium Hospitality Operations & Infrastructure Venue Manager during tournament time. She/he will work closely with the Official Hospitality Provider and FIFA’s stadium operations and infrastructure functional areas to ensure contractual and requirements compliance.

The main responsibilities and oversights of the Hospitality Operations and Venue Services Manager for the FIFA Women´s World Cup 2027™ include:

- Responsible for the management and operational readiness and delivery of the Affiliates and Commercial Hospitality programmes, reporting duties, maintenance/creation of operational and infrastructure documentations, etc;
- Ensuring Infrastructure readiness and maintenance services of Hospitality areas, in close cooperation with the FIFA other functional areas, the Official Hospitality Provider (OHP) and Stadium Authorities;
- Responsible for the on-site management of the Official Hospitality Provider (OHP) and their suppliers, and Hospitality Volunteers;
- Checking and validating the Operational plans from the service-providing departments to Hospitality (Cleaning and Waste, Security, Medical, Signage, Transport, Fan Operations, Accreditation, Power, IT, TV, ticketing, etc.);
- Ensuring excellent service to the FIFA Affiliates on site, overlooking the set-up and readiness of their facilities, monitoring service delivery from the Official Hospitality Provider (OHP) from the set-up phase through to match day delivery of services;
- Ensuring contractual deliverables to the FIFA Commercial Affiliates and to the Official Hospitality Provider (OHP);
- Overall on-site hospitality guest management;
- Ensure service consistency throughout the different hospitality programmes across all matches in the venue;
- Validating all on-site hospitality directional signage;
- Ensuring Health and Safety regulations are strictly observed and respected by the Official Hospitality Provider (OHP);
- Ensuring Hospitality guest numbers are updated and shared with all relevant FIFA stakeholders;
- Ensuring that all stakeholders are appropriately accredited. Manage the distribution of SADs (supplementary access devices) to all relevant functional areas, restricting access to hospitality areas as needed;
- Ensure the catering service runs as expected in the Affiliates and Commercial Hospitality programmes;
- Handling all hospitality related issues on Match Day;
- Attend the FIFA Daily Coordination Meeting at the Venue and hold daily Hospitality Team Meetings with the Official Hospitality Provider (OHP);
- Reporting on a daily basis to the FIFA HQ, reporting issues in good time.

Education & Qualifications

- Bachelor’s Degree or similar level of education in Event Management, Sports Hospitality Management, Project Management, etc.

Work Experience

- Minimum of 5 years of work experience in stadium hospitality or venue management, managing several venues simultaneously, preferably for major sports or entertainment events;
- Proven experience with event overlay (including provision of temporary power and water), ticketing, dressing and signage, catering, logistics and security operations;
- Proven experience managing multiple service providers, particularly for Technical services, Cleaning and Waste services, Security Services, Access control Services, Accreditation, etc;
- Strong communication and interpersonal skills;
- Strong customer-service attitude, even when under pressure;
- Ability to work independently and in a team across simultaneous work streams;
- Exquisite organizational skills;
- Ability to lead, manage, and motivate a team.

Languages

- Fluent in Portuguese and English. Additional languages considered an asset.

Technology

- Proficient in MS Office (Excel, Word, PowerPoint, Visio & Project) and planning software and online collaboration tools;
- Excellent knowledge of AutoCAD and literacy of architectural drawings.

FIFA has established a Local FIFA Subsidiary in Brazil to work together with FIFA Zurich to deliver the biggest women’s sporting event in the world, the FIFA Women’s World Cup 2027™ (“FWWC2027”) that for the first time ever, is hosted in South America in Brazil. Now is your time to be part of the workforce that is creating this unique and unforgettable experience.
Please submit your CV in English, as it will be reviewed by an international team.
Reporting organizationally to the Ticketing Customer Relationship Senior Manager the Ticketing Member Associations Customer Care Manager will help serve Ticketing and Hospitality efforts for the FIFA Women’s World Cup 2027™. This role will be responsible for planning and management of the customer care strategies and processes for Group Sales Customers to specifically fulfil all FIFA’s Member Associations ticketing requirements and ensure a smooth and successful ticketing operation for these key FIFA stakeholders. The Customer Care Manager must ensure compliance with the applicable sales strategy and the FIFA ticketing requirements, policies and regulations whilst providing support to all Member Associations with ticketing issues and enquiries. The Customer Care Manager focuses particularly on the delivery of effective ticketing customer care for the FIFA Women’s World Cup 2027.
- Plan and implement effective customer care strategies and processes across all the established communications channels (email, phone and any other ticketing bespoke systems);
- Train and manage a small team, in line with the sales strategy and FIFA ticketing requirements, policies and regulations; including regular quality assurance checks;
- Perform customer care ticketing processes (back office and onsite) whenever required;
- Build, manage and maintain successful relationships with all FIFA’s Member Associations whilst resolving all issues and enquiries;
- Manage and monitor the ticket quota and requests allocated to FIFA Member Associations;
- Issue all necessary ticketing communications and be able to translate into required languages, where applicable;
- Present ticketing information to Member Associations and other stakeholders both in person and online;
- Plan effective communication and escalation processes and ensure implementation within the team;
- Plan and implement quality control procedures to ensure that any deviation from the requirements is detected and corrected as soon as possible;
- Actively research and implement solutions to pro-actively increase the productivity of the group sales customer care team, and maximise customer information and satisfaction;
- Analyse and report regularly on KPIs and the effectiveness of customer care being delivered;
- Pro-actively identify and report on patterns and risks, and implement processes to mitigate them;
- Ensure that all customer care processes are in compliance with the different FIFA functional areas requirements, including but not limited to Legal, Sustainability, Data Protection, Finance, etc.;
- Liaise with internal and external stakeholders to ensure the relevant customer care information is available and share applicable knowledge;
- Ensure an efficient administration and archive of all versions of customer care and knowledge base, in all languages;
- Report on the implementation of sales strategy and ticketing requirements;
- Ensure adherence to specific operational deadlines and project plans and compliance with ticketing policies, regulations and GDPR.
SKILLS FRAMEWORK
ACCOUNTABILITY: Demonstrate commitment to responsibilities and objectively analyse one’s behaviour, while assuming consequences of one’s own actions and/or decisions and learning from one’s mistakes.
DECISION MAKING: Ability to identify and swiftly make decisions in critical situations, take initiative and calculate risks, explore alternative solutions, and respond promptly to unforeseen circumstances.
INCLUSIVITY:Achieve shared organizational objectives by sharing information with colleagues across all levels and divisions, tangibly influencing others, and maintaining a network of support contacts.
INITIATIVE: Capacity to break new ground, look for unconventional solutions, and produce fresh ideas.
INNOVATION: Capacity to break new ground, look for unconventional solutions, and produce fresh ideas.
LEADERSHIP:Ability to lead one’s contacts/colleagues/partners, encourage teamwork, and delegate authority / decision-making power, as needed, to produce the expected results and make efficient use of the team’s skills and talents.
VISION: Ability to perceive the organization's global environmental impact, anticipate decision consequences, grasp organizational missions, and formulate strategic plans.
EDUCATION & QUALIFICATIONS
Bachelor's or Master's degree or equivalent in relevant areas.
WORK EXPERIENCE
- Planning and delivery of a similar project for a major international sport event - Planning and delivery of Customer Care for corporate customers/business stakeholders - Leading and managing small teams - Delivery of user acceptance tests - Ticketing - Venue and onsite operations experience for major sports event - Customer Service - Excellent communication and relationship management - Good numeracy - Courtesy and Cooperation - Accountability and Transparency - Analysis and Innovation - Flexibility and Adaptability - Perseverance and Dedication - Proactivity and Organisation - Time Management and Prioritisation
LANGUAGES
Fluent in English and Portuguese, spoken and written.
Fluent in Spanish, French or German, spoken and written.
TECHNOLOGY
- Proficient in MS Office (Excel, Word, PowerPoint, Monday) and planning software and online collaboration tools - CRM software for case management, including automatic and manual management of the cases.
Certifications & Requirements
- Ability to re-locate to Rio de Janeiro - Right to work in Brazil

FIFA has established a Local FIFA Subsidiary in Brazil to work together with FIFA Zurich to deliver the biggest women’s sporting event in the world, the FIFA Women’s World Cup 2027™ (“FWWC2027”) that for the first time ever, is hosted in South America in Brazil. Now is your time to be part of the workforce that is creating this unique and unforgettable experience.

Please submit your CV in English, as it will be reviewed by an international team.

Reporting organizationally to the Ticketing Customer Relationship Senior Manager, the Ticketing Commercial Partners & Local Entities Customer Care Manager will help serve Ticketing and Hospitality efforts for the FIFA Women’s World Cup 2027™. This role will be responsible for planning and management of the customer care strategies and processes for Group Sales Customers to specifically fulfil all FIFA’s Commercial Partners and Local Entities ticketing requirements and ensure a smooth and successful ticketing operation for these key FIFA stakeholders.

The Customer Care Manager must ensure compliance with the applicable sales strategy and the FIFA ticketing requirements, policies and regulations whilst providing support to all FIFA’s Commercial Partners with ticketing issues and enquiries. Focuses particularly on the delivery of effective ticketing customer care for the FIFA Women’s World Cup 2027™.

- Plan and implement effective customer care strategies and processes across all the established communications channels (email, phone and any other ticketing bespoke systems);

- Perform user acceptance tests for ticket sales, distribution and communication channels in pre-production and production, concentrating on mobile ticketing processes to ensure effective customer care and management of Commercial Partners and Local Entities’ requirements

- Train and manage a small team, in line with the sales strategy and FIFA ticketing requirements, policies and regulations; including regular quality assurance checks;

- Perform customer care ticketing processes (back office and onsite) whenever required;

- Build, manage and maintain successful relationships with all FIFA Commercial Partners and Local Entities (Partners, Sponsors, Licensees, Host Cities, etc.) whilst resolving all issues and enquiries;

- Manage and monitor the ticket quota and requests allocated to FIFA Commercial Partners and Local Entities;

- Issue all necessary ticketing communications and be able to translate into required languages, where applicable;

- Present ticketing information and deliver training to Commercial Partners and Local Entities, and other stakeholders both in person and online;

- Plan effective communication and escalation processes and ensure implementation within the team;

- Plan and implement quality control procedures to ensure that any deviation from the ticketing requirements and system requirements is detected and corrected as soon as possible;

- Actively research and implement solutions to pro-actively increase the productivity of the group sales customer care team, and maximize customer information and satisfaction;

- Analyse and report regularly on KPIs and the effectiveness of customer care being delivered

- Pro-actively identify and report on patterns and risks, and implement processes to mitigate them;

- Ensure that all customer care processes are in compliance with the different FIFA functional areas requirements, including but not limited to Legal, Sustainability, Data Protection, Finance, etc.;

- Liaise with internal and external stakeholders to ensure the relevant customer care information is available and share applicable knowledge;

- Ensure an efficient administration and archive of all versions of customer care and knowledge base, in all languages;

- Report on the implementation of sales strategy and ticketing requirements; plus results of testing of ticket sales, distribution and communication channels including mobile ticketing;

- Ensure adherence to specific operational deadlines and project plans and compliance with ticketing policies, regulations and GDPR.

SKILLS FRAMEWORK

ACCOUNTABILITY: Demonstrate commitment to responsibilities and objectively analyse one’s behaviour, while assuming consequences of one’s own actions and/or decisions and learning from one’s mistakes.

DECISION MAKING: Ability to identify and swiftly make decisions in critical situations, take initiative and calculate risks, explore alternative solutions, and respond promptly to unforeseen circumstances.

INCLUSIVITY:Achieve shared organizational objectives by sharing information with colleagues across all levels and divisions, tangibly influencing others, and maintaining a network of support contacts.

INITIATIVE: Capacity to break new ground, look for unconventional solutions, and produce fresh ideas.

INNOVATION: Capacity to break new ground, look for unconventional solutions, and produce fresh ideas.

LEADERSHIP:Ability to lead one’s contacts/colleagues/partners, encourage teamwork, and delegate authority / decision-making power, as needed, to produce the expected results and make efficient use of the team’s skills and talents.

VISION: Ability to perceive the organization's global environmental impact, anticipate decision consequences, grasp organizational missions, and formulate strategic plans.

EDUCATION & QUALIFICATIONS

Bachelor's or Master's degree or equivalent in relevant areas.

WORK EXPERIENCE

- Planning and delivery of a similar project during a previous FIFA World Cup;
- Planning and delivery of Customer Care for corporate customers/business stakeholders;
- Leading and managing small teams;
- Delivery of user acceptance tests;
- Ticketing;
- Venue and onsite operations experience for major sports event, including a previous FIFA World Cup;
- Customer Service;
- Excellent communication and relationship management;
- Good numeracy;
- Courtesy and Cooperation;
- Accountability and Transparency;
- Analysis and Innovation;
- Flexibility and Adaptability;
- Perseverance and Dedication;
- Proactivity and Organisation;
- Time Management and Prioritisation;

LANGUAGES

Fluent in English and Portuguese, spoken and written.

Spanish and/or additional languages is highly advantageous.

TECHNOLOGY

- Proficient in MS Office (Excel, Word, PowerPoint, Monday) and planning software and online collaboration tools

- CRM software for case management, including automatic and manual management of the cases.

Certifications & Requirements

- Ability to re-locate to Rio de Janeiro
- Right to work in Brazil

job.html_description:
 The Academy Driver is responsible for providing a safe, reliable and professional driving service across. the Academy. Reporting to the Head of Academy Operations, the role includes, management of part-time drivers (exclusively Academy), and to work alongside the Club Driver &amp; Fleet Compliance Manager ensuring all vehicles are maintained and presented to a professional standard. The Academy Driver delivers a consistent, reliable service to ensure safe transport of Academy players, staff and guests.<br><br>This will be a part-time (20-hour) role, with hours split across a 7-day week.&nbsp;
<h3>Responsibilities</h3><ul><li>Provide transport for identified registered players to and from our Motspur Park training site.</li><li>Provide transport for trialist players to and from airports, train stations, accommodation, and club activities.</li><li>Support the player induction process when identifying players in need of transport support.</li><li>Act as a guide for visits to Motspur Park and Craven Cottage.</li><li>Assist the club on 1st team match days for corporate driving requirement.</li><li>Support the Academy across key events and wider activities.</li><li>Promote the work of Fulham Academy amongst the London football community.</li><li>Always represent Fulham Football Club to a high standard in line with club values.</li></ul>
<h3>Requirements</h3><ul><li>Hold a full clean driving licence</li><li>Interact with others in a positive manner</li><li>Strong understanding of the local area</li><li>Positive ability to work within a diverse organisation</li><li>Self-starter who takes pride in the delivery of a professional service</li><li>Bi-Lingual (Desired)</li><li>D1 driving licence (Desired)</li></ul>

 Oversee the efficient receipt, storage, dispatch and movements of all stock. Be able to ensure productivity targets are achieved and that all warehouse processes are running smoothly and promptly. Delivering of Stock to the store.&nbsp;<br><br>This role is 24 hours per week: shifts on Monday, Tuesday and Friday.&nbsp;
<h3>Responsibilities</h3>Below are example responsibilities but this is not intended to be an exhaustive list:<br><ul><li>Driving between sites to deliver retail stock as and when required.</li><li>Control retail stock movements</li><li>Responsible for pick, pack and dispatch in the online retail store.</li><li>Ensure product is stored in a safe and responsible manner.</li><li>Support Retail team in all aspects of stock and movements.</li><li>Support internet and online team.</li><li>Strategically manage warehouse in compliance with company’s policies and vision</li><li>Implement and adhere to all Club procedures ensuring all staff are fully aware and always trained</li><li>Uphold all retail security procedures, working closely with the Warehouse team</li><li>Support and reflect the Club Values on a day-to-day basis, ensuring the team are also demonstrating the appropriate behaviours</li><li>Proactively seek to build and maintain relationships with appropriate people in the business, and build the profile of the retail operation</li></ul><br><strong><u>Key Skills:</u></strong><br><ul><li>A strong communication skill at all levels both oral and written</li><li>Strong interpersonal skills and confidence in dealing with people at all levels of the organisation</li><li>Pragmatic and flexible approach</li><li>Work well under pressure through very busy trading periods</li><li>Team player with a hands-on approach</li><li>Know how to do Shirt printings&nbsp;</li><li>The ability to drive a van for delivery purposes</li></ul><br>&nbsp;
<h3>Requirements</h3><strong><u>Essential:</u></strong><br><br><strong>Experience:</strong><br>· Retail Systems<br>· Administrative background<br>· Driving – full clean driving licence<br><br><strong>Skills, Knowledge &amp; Qualifications:</strong><br>· GCSE level Educated<br>· PC literate<br><br><strong>Personal Qualities:</strong><br>· Enthusiastic and creative<br>· Reliable And Dedicated<br>· Respect for confidentiality<br>· Flexible attitude to work tasks<br><br><strong><u>Preferred:</u></strong><br><br><strong>Experience:</strong><br>· Retail Product Knowledge<br>&nbsp;· Online Retail Skills<br>&nbsp;· Retail Operations environment&nbsp;<br>&nbsp;· Shirt Printing<br><br><strong>Skills, Knowledge &amp; Qualifications:&nbsp;</strong><br>· Retail software / system

 Fulham FC Foundation are currently seeking to recruit an enthusiastic and committed person to take up the casual position of DisAbility Football &amp; Sports Coach.<br><br>Reporting directly to our Senior DisAbility Development Manager, the DisAbility Football &amp; Sports Coaches are responsible for delivering high-quality football &amp; sports coaching to children, young people and adults with disabilities and additional needs. This role involves delivery across a wide-range of our DisAbility Programmes, including Pan DisAbility Clubs, Active Autism, Down’s Syndrome ‘Badgers’, Blind and Partially Sighted, Cerebral Palsy and Dwarfism Football Sessions. In addition there will be opportunities to work in our DisAbility Schools programme delivering PE, Enrichment Activities and After School Clubs.<br><br>While the primary focus of this role is on DisAbility Football &amp; Sport, there may be opportunities to contribute to other FFC Foundation activities such as Skills Club, Development Centres, Soccer Schools, Primary Education, Kicks, and Health &amp; Wellbeing. We would encourage candidates to prioritise DisAbility Programmes where possible, while remaining flexible to support other areas as needed.<br><br>This is a casual role where flexibility is essential, as the role necessitates involvement in supporting the delivery of programme activities as and when required. &nbsp;<br><br>The successful candidate will be somebody who has prior experience delivering football &amp; sports coaching sessions to children &amp; young people with disabilities or additional needs in grassroots &amp; school settings, holds at least a FA Level 1/Introduction to Coaching Football qualification and is committed to the charitable purpose of Fulham FC Foundation.<br><br>As this role is casual, there is no set timetable. Sessions may be offered on an adhoc or regular basis, depending on the needs of Fulham FC Foundation. It is the responsibility of the DisAbility Football &amp; Sports Coaches to maintain consistent and effective communication with our Senior DisAbility Development Manager and Operations Officers to ensure the continuation of work.<br><br>Whilst there is no obligation for Fulham FC Foundation to provide, or for the DisAbility Football &amp; Sports Coaches to accept, work. DisAbility Football &amp; Sports Coaches who do not work for an extended period of time, will be deactivated.<br><br>The successful candidates should be available to work across at least one of the below times, in order to receive work. We are extremely keen to hear from those who are able to work on Saturday mornings.<br><br>Weekdays – 9am to 5 pm;<br>Weekday Evenings – 5pm to 9pm<br>Weekends – Saturdays – 8am to 12noon.<br>Work in other timings is available, however on a far reduced frequency.<br>Salary Range: £12.95 p/h to £16.50 p/h<br><br><strong>Next steps</strong>:<br>There is no closing date for this role. Applications will be reviewed on a bi-weekly basis.<br><br><strong>If successful, you will join a vibrant team who are passionate about achieving the organisation's vision of “an active, inclusive and thriving community”, and you’ll have the opportunity to build on your existing skills through a variety of training and development opportunities and experiences</strong><br>*<strong>This job description should not be regarded as exclusive or exhaustive. It is intended as an outline indication of areas of activity and responsibility and will be amended in the light of the changing needs of the organisation</strong>.
<h3>Responsibilities</h3><ul><li>To act as an Ambassador for Fulham FC Foundation (FFCF), representing the organisation professionally in line with its values.</li><li>To plan and deliver high-quality football and sports coaching sessions to children, young people &amp; adults in-line with FFCF standards.</li><li>To provide a safe, positive and inclusive learning environment at all times,</li><li>To adhere to FFCF’s safeguarding policies and procedures, ensuring the timely reporting of any safeguarding concerns or incidents within sessions.</li><li>To engage, include, inspire and grow participation across FFCF activities.</li><li>To support the transition of participants between different FFCF programmes and activities.</li><li>To champion opportunities for individuals from underrepresented groups within FFCF activities.&nbsp;</li><li>To identify and support progression pathways for talented young people.&nbsp;</li><li>To support the development of FFCF programmes through positive collaboration with Department Managers / Operations Officers.&nbsp;</li><li>To support the promotion of FFCF programmes across the local community.</li><li>&nbsp;To assist in data collection and completion of monitoring &amp; evaluation on an ongoing basis.</li></ul>&nbsp;<br>&nbsp;<br>&nbsp;
<h3>Requirements</h3>Essential:<br>Experience:<br><ul><li>Delivery of football coaching sessions in a grassroots environment</li><li>Delivery of sports coaching sessions to children, young people or adults with disabilities and additional needs.</li><li>Delivery within a school/college setting.</li><li>Working in a customer-facing role.</li></ul><br>Skills, Knowledge &amp; Qualifications:<br><ul><li>Introduction to Coaching Football qualification</li><li>In-date FA Emergency First Aid</li><li>In-date FA Safeguarding Children certificate</li><li>Base knowledge of and willingness to learn &amp; contribute towards FFCF strategic aims.</li></ul><br>Personal Qualities:<br><ul><li>A positive role-model for children &amp; young people.</li><li>Ability to travel independently across South-West London, including transport of equipment.</li><li>Well presented, with a professional manner.</li><li>Positive, energetic persona. Able to build rapport with participants.</li><li>Excellent time-keeping &amp; punctuality.</li><li>Willingness to learn &amp; develop personally &amp; professionally.</li></ul><br>Preferred:<br>Experience:<br><ul><li>Delivery of football &amp; sports coaching sessions in a Club Community Organisation (CCO).</li><li>Delivery of Physical Education within a school setting.</li><li>Delivery within a classroom environment.</li><li>Marketing &amp; Promoting participation activities in the community.</li><li>Delivery of football &amp; sports coaching sessions to females.</li></ul><br>Skills, Knowledge &amp; Qualifications:<br><ul><li>FA Level 2/UEFA C in Coaching Football qualification (or higher).</li><li>Additional PE/HLTA qualification</li><li>Mentoring qualification</li><li>Non-football NGB sports qualifications.</li></ul>

 Great organisations are built by great people, and we're looking for a talented&nbsp;Talent Acquisition Lead&nbsp;to help us find and attract the very best.<br>&nbsp;<br>Founded in 1879, Fulham Football Club is London’s oldest professional football club and one of the most historic names in English football. Based at the iconic Craven Cottage on the banks of the River Thames, Fulham FC competes in the Premier League and operates at the intersection of elite sport, global entertainment and community heritage. The Club is part of a wider sporting and business group and combines a deep respect for tradition with modern, progressive ambition. Fulham FC is proud of its loyal fanbase, strong community roots and growing international profile.<br>&nbsp;<br>Our Vision is to be a progressive Premier League club that balances sporting success with long-term stability, commercial growth and a positive impact on our people, supporters and community.<br>&nbsp;<br>Working at Fulham FC is fast-paced, collaborative and purpose-driven. Employees are united by a shared passion for football and pride in representing a historic Club. The culture blends the intensity and accountability of elite sport with a supportive, professional working environment. People are expected to be adaptable, resilient and solutions-focused, while leaders are encouraged to empower, develop and inspire their teams. Fulham FC values diversity, inclusion and wellbeing, and is committed to creating an environment where people can perform at their best and feel a strong sense of belonging.<br>&nbsp;<br>This is a new role, and you'll lead our recruitment strategy, partner with business leaders, champion an exceptional candidate experience, and help shape our employer brand. This role offers the opportunity to influence how we attract talent and support the growth of our organisation.<br>&nbsp;<br>We're looking for someone who:<br>&nbsp;<br><ul><li>Thinks strategically and acts proactively.</li><li>Builds strong relationships across the business.</li><li>Enjoys finding innovative ways to attract talent.</li><li>Is passionate about diversity, inclusion, and candidate experience.</li><li>Thrives in a fast-paced and collaborative environment.</li></ul>&nbsp;<br>If you're looking for a role where you can truly make a difference, we'd love to hear from you.<br><br>
<h3>Responsibilities</h3><em>The Talent Acquisition Lead should possess:&nbsp;</em><br><ul><li>Significant experience in talent acquisition, recruitment or resourcing leadership.&nbsp;</li><li>Proven ability to develop and implement talent acquisition strategies.&nbsp;</li><li>Experience managing multiple recruitment campaigns across varied disciplines.&nbsp;</li><li>Strong stakeholder management and influencing skills.&nbsp;</li><li>Knowledge of employment legislation and recruitment compliance requirements.&nbsp;</li><li>Experience using recruitment technologies.&nbsp;</li><li>Strong analytical and reporting capabilities.</li><li>Be able to work independently and proactively.&nbsp;</li></ul>&nbsp;<br><em>It is desirable that the role holder possess:&nbsp;</em><br><ul><li>CIPD qualification or equivalent HR qualification.&nbsp;</li><li>Experience leading recruitment transformation projects.&nbsp;</li><li>Experience supporting organisational growth or restructuring programmes.&nbsp;</li><li>Knowledge of employer branding and recruitment marketing techniques.</li></ul>&nbsp;<br>Note: The Talent Acquisition Lead does not need to be a Fulham fan, a football fan or even a fan of sport! &nbsp;We want the best person for the job, not the person who knows the most about football. &nbsp;In any case, we are confident that you will become a Fulham fan before long! &nbsp; &nbsp;&nbsp;<br>&nbsp;
<h3>Requirements</h3>Working as the Talent Acquisition Lead for a Premier League football club is a unique role. &nbsp;It is responsible for developing and delivering the organisation's talent acquisition strategy to attract, engage and hire high-quality talent. The role leads all recruitment activities, ensuring a proactive and commercially focused approach to workforce planning, employer branding, candidate experience and selection processes.<br>&nbsp;<br>The Talent Acquisition Lead partners closely with all business leaders to understand current and future workforce needs, build talent pipelines and ensure recruitment practices support organisational growth, diversity and inclusion objectives, compliance requirements and employer brand positioning.<br>&nbsp;<br>The following is a non-exhaustive list of the responsibilities of the role:&nbsp;<br>&nbsp;<br><em>Talent Acquisition Strategy</em><br><ul><li>Develop and implement a talent acquisition strategy aligned to business objectives and workforce plans.</li><li>Identify current and future talent requirements across all business areas.</li><li>Lead recruitment planning activities to support organisational growth and succession needs.&nbsp;</li><li>Monitor labour market trends and provide insight on recruitment challenges and opportunities.</li><li>Drive continuous improvement in recruitment practices and candidate attraction methods.</li></ul>&nbsp;<br><em>Recruitment Delivery</em><br><ul><li>Lead end-to-end recruitment activity across all functions and levels.</li><li>Ensure vacancies are managed efficiently with a focus on quality, time-to-hire and cost-effectiveness.</li><li>Partner with hiring managers to define role requirements and recruitment strategies.</li><li>Oversee candidate sourcing, screening, interviewing and selection processes.</li><li>Support recruitment for critical, specialist and senior-level positions.</li></ul>&nbsp;<br><em>Stakeholder Management</em><br><ul><li>Build strong relationships with senior leaders and hiring managers.</li><li>Act as a trusted advisor on recruitment best practice and market intelligence.</li><li>Challenge and influence stakeholders to ensure effective hiring decisions.</li><li>Provide regular recruitment updates and reporting to leaders and HR stakeholders.</li></ul>&nbsp;<br><em>Employer Branding and Attraction</em><br><ul><li>Lead initiatives to strengthen the organisation's employer brand.</li><li>Develop recruitment marketing campaigns to attract diverse talent pools.</li><li>Enhance candidate engagement through a positive recruitment experience.</li><li>Promote the organisation through careers sites, social media, networking events and partnerships.</li></ul>&nbsp;<br><em>Talent Pipeline Development</em><br><ul><li>Establish and maintain talent pools for key and hard-to-fill roles.</li><li>Develop proactive sourcing strategies to reduce dependency on reactive recruitment.</li><li>Build relationships with educational institutions, professional bodies and industry networks.</li><li>Support talent mapping and succession planning activities.</li></ul><em>&nbsp;<br>Diversity, Equity and Inclusion</em><br><ul><li>Ensure recruitment practices promote equality, diversity and inclusion.</li><li>Monitor diversity data throughout recruitment processes.</li><li>Identify and implement initiatives to improve diverse candidate attraction and hiring outcomes.</li><li>Train managers on inclusive recruitment and selection techniques.</li></ul>&nbsp;<br><em>Recruitment Operations and Compliance</em><br><ul><li>Ensure recruitment activity complies with employment legislation and organisational policies.</li><li>Oversee and improve recruitment systems, processes and governance requirements.</li><li>Maintain accurate recruitment records and regular reporting.</li><li>Ensure right-to-work, background screening and onboarding requirements are completed appropriately and in a timely manner.</li><li>Review and update recruitment policies and procedures.</li></ul>&nbsp;<br><em>Workforce Planning</em><br><ul><li>Support organisational workforce planning and organisational change activities.</li><li>Provide recruitment data and insights to inform strategic workforce decisions.</li><li>Identify anticipated skills shortages and recommend mitigation strategies.</li><li>Collaborate with HR colleagues on retention and talent management initiatives.</li></ul>&nbsp;
<h3>Benefits</h3>We expect to close applications on 17th September, but if we receive a high level of interest, we may close the vacancy sooner. To avoid disappointment, please submit your application at the earliest opportunity.<br><br>

 In this role, you will work as part of the Ticket Office team at Craven Cottage to manage inbound enquiries across a number of different communication channels – phone, email, online and in person – and deliver on the sale of commercial products relating to Fulham Football Club through the Club’s ticketing system, Ticketmaster. &nbsp;<br id="isPasted">&nbsp;&nbsp;<br>The Ticket Office team form a critical part of the sales structure of the business, and you will be required to proactively support the Club in its objective to make it easy for people to buy from Fulham FC by assisting with supporter queries on our busy matchdays. &nbsp;<br>&nbsp;&nbsp;<br>You will form part of the team working as the first line of contact for our fans’ inquiries and as such we expect a high level of customer service and support at all times. &nbsp;<br>&nbsp;<br>You will be asked to provide assistance to the Head of Ticketing and the Deputy Supporter Centre Manager with a variety of Ticket Office duties as required. A good level of communication will be required. &nbsp;
<h3>Responsibilities</h3><strong>The Ticketing and Membership Executive - Match Days must have:&nbsp;</strong><ul><li>Customer Service experience</li><li>A good IT and technology systems understanding</li><li>Competent with all Microsoft Office Products</li><li>Ability to deal with the public with a focus on service excellence&nbsp;</li><li>Able to work under pressure&nbsp;</li><li>Ability to communicate with and relate to staff members at all levels&nbsp;</li><li>Work on own initiative / creative&nbsp;</li><li>Respect for confidentiality&nbsp;</li><li>Flexible attitude to work tasks&nbsp;</li><li>Genuine commitment to provide high quality customer service&nbsp;</li><li>Positive ‘can do’ approach&nbsp;</li><li>Desire to learn with enthusiasm</li></ul><br><strong>Ideally, The Ticketing and Membership Executive - Match Days will have:&nbsp;</strong><ul><li>Previous experience with Ticketing Systems</li><li>Experience in a sales role</li></ul>
<h3>Requirements</h3><strong>The following is a non-exhaustive list of the responsibilities of the role:&nbsp;</strong><ul><li>Providing service excellence when dealing with the Clubs customers (supporters, staff etc), at all times, serving customers in a polite, courteous and professional manner &nbsp;</li><li>Handling any customer queries and complaints with a solution driven and positive approach &nbsp;</li><li>Processing all ticket sales for Fulham FC products, away games and supporter travel, with daily reconciliation of all sales through the Ticketmaster system &nbsp;&nbsp;</li><li>Updating and maintaining supporter database records to ensure data is accurately captured across the Ticketing System (Ticketmaster) and CRM System &nbsp;</li><li>This role will be required to work all home league matchdays – on evenings or weekends , and an other ad-hoc fixtures or events as required &nbsp;&nbsp;</li><li>You may also be required to carry out other tasks, not listed, to assist in the efficient operation of our business. &nbsp;At all times you will be required to act in accordance with FFC company policies, follow departmental procedures and maintain the highest level of confidentiality. &nbsp;<strong><br></strong></li></ul>

 Fulham FC Foundation is seeking a creative part-time Graphic Designer to support the communications of Fulham FC’s official charity. This role will work across a wide range of digital and print design projects, helping to bring the Foundation’s visual identity to life across all programmes and activities.<br><br>Working within established brand guidelines, you will contribute to digital campaigns and front‑end design projects, while also bringing your own creativity and ideas to each brief. Design direction will be provided, but the ability to work independently will be key to success in this role.<br><br>If you are passionate about design, looking for a new challenge, and feel you can add value to our team, please visit hhtp://careers.fulhamfc.com/<br>&nbsp;<br><em>*This job description should not be regarded as exclusive or exhaustive. It is intended as an outline indication of areas of activity and responsibility and will be amended in the light of the changing needs of the organisation</em>.<br><br>Closing date for applications is Wednesday 5 August 2026.<br><br>Salary range: £20k-£22.5k<br>&nbsp;<br>First stage interviews will take place across Thursday 13th &amp; Friday 14th August 2026, and second stage interviews will take place on Thursday 20th August 2026. Please ensure you are available to interview on these dates prior to applying.<br><br>The post is subject to an enhanced Disclosure and Barring Service check.<br><br>Fulham Football Club Foundation is committed to increasing diversity and maintaining an inclusive workplace culture. We welcome applications from all qualified candidates regardless of ethnicity, race, gender, religious belief, sexual orientation, age, marital status, or disability.<br><br>Applicants must have the right to live and work in the United Kingdom and be able to provide appropriate documentation for the duration of their employment.<br><br><br>
<h3>Responsibilities</h3>Your responsibilities will include, but are not limited to:<br><br>• Designing and building digital assets, including social media graphics, flyers, presentations, and newsletters<br>• Implementing design briefs in line with the Foundation’s brand guidelines<br>• Supporting and contributing to the development of the Foundation’s visual identity across multiple platforms and mediums<br>• Managing multiple design briefs from concept through to final delivery<br>• Working to tight deadlines while following efficient resourcing and scheduling processes<br>• Supporting social media scheduling and posting across Foundation channels<br>• Assisting with asset management and the printing of marketing collateral
<h3>Requirements</h3><strong>The successful candidate will:</strong><br>• Be able to manage multiple briefs and work under pressure to tight deadlines<br>• Demonstrate a strong portfolio showcasing a range of print and digital design work for varied audiences<br>• Have advanced working knowledge of Adobe Creative Suite, including Photoshop, Illustrator, and InDesign, as well as PowerPoint<br>• Hold a design‑related degree, or demonstrate equivalent experience through a strong portfolio<br>• Ideally have experience working within sport, community, or charitable organisations<br>&nbsp;<br><strong>Personal attributes</strong><br>We are looking for a team player who is:<br>• Open to feedback and able to collaborate effectively<br>• Highly organised with strong attention to detail<br>• Able to problem‑solve independently<br>• Capable of blending creative vision with strategic thinking<br>• Values in-person collaboration and team culture (the role is office based)<br>&nbsp;

job.plain_text_description:
Envie de rejoindre un Groupe unique et ambitieux ?

Grâce à un modèle économique articulé autour du football masculin et ouvert sur l'international, Eagle Football Group, propriétaire de l'Olympique Lyonnais se démarque dans le paysage français du sport professionnel.

Propriétaire de notre Stade, nous avons à cœur de respecter les enjeux socio-économiques tout en étant un acteur responsable et engagé dans la vie locale.

Notre dynamisme incarné par notre équipe masculine et notre Academy mixte nous incite à innover sans cesse et à nous adapter aux profonds changements de notre coeur de métier.

Nous recherchons un(e) Juriste (H/F) en CDD de remplacement à pourvoir dès à présent.

Vous serez rattaché(e) à la Direction Juridique, sous la responsabilité de la Responsable Juridique.

Véritable acteur de la sécurisation juridique des activités du Groupe, vous intervenez sur un périmètre varié couvrant la gestion des assurances, les contrats commerciaux et techniques, ainsi que le suivi des contentieux.

Votre objectif sera donc de protéger et d'accompagner le développement du Groupe en assurant le pilotage des contrats d'assurance et des sinistres, la rédaction et la négociation des contrats liés à l'exploitation des infrastructures, ainsi que la gestion des pré-contentieux et de la veille juridique.

Dans ce cadre, vos missions seront les suivantes :

- Assurances

- Suivi des contrats d’assurance Groupe (RC, multirisques, cyber, construction flotte auto…) ;
- Lancement et suivi des appels d’offres, revue et négociation des polices ;
- Souscription de nouveaux contrats selon les besoins opérationnels ;
- Déclarations et suivi des sinistres en lien avec les services internes et les assureurs.

- Contrats commerciaux

- Rédaction, révision et négociation de contrats en particulier : contrats techniques en lien avec la gestion des infrastructures, tels que des contrats de prestations de services, contrats d’exploitation/maintenance, baux, NDA… ;
- Suivi de l’exécution des contrats en coordination avec les équipes métiers, gestion des relations contractuelles et des renouvellements.

- Contentieux et veille juridique

- Préparation des mises en demeure, rédaction de protocoles transactionnels ;
- Suivi des pré-contentieux et contentieux en lien avec le périmètre d’activités ;
- Veille juridique et réglementaire en droit des affaires et des assurances.

- Support transversal

- Participation aux projets juridiques du Groupe ;
- Actualisation des ressources documentaires.

PROFIL:

Vous justifiez d’un Bac +5 (Droit des Assurances ou Droit des Affaires) et d’une expérience de 5 à 10 ans en entreprise, cabinet ou courtage, avec une forte composante commerciale.

Nous recherchons les compétences techniques suivantes :

- Maîtrise du droit des assurances et du droit des contrats ;
- Excellentes capacités rédactionnelles et de négociation ;
- Maîtrise des outils bureautiques (Word, Excel, PowerPoint) ;
- Appétence pour les outils digitaux de gestion contractuelle et IA juridique ;
- Anglais juridique courant (écrit et oral).

Nous apprécierons également vos qualités personnelles telles que votre agilité intellectuelle, votre esprit d’analyse et de synthèse ainsi que votre sens du relationnel et du travail en équipe, permettant de vous adapter à des environnements/métiers divers et d’avoir une véritable orientation business.

Tous les postes sont ouverts aux personnes en situation de handicap.

Pour vous donner un avant-goût de votre quotidien parmi nous, voici quelques-uns de nos avantages :

- Une vraie qualité de vie au travail, au cœur de notre politique RH (partenariat avec une salle de sport à proximité des bureaux, nombreux évènements conviviaux organisés tout au long de l’année, une assistance sociale à votre disposition) ;
- Un parcours d’intégration unique ;
- La possibilité de s’impliquer dans des actions sociales et solidaires.

Convaincu(e) ? N’hésitez plus, postulez !

Envie de rejoindre un Groupe unique et ambitieux ?

Grâce à un modèle économique articulé autour du football masculin et ouvert sur l'international, Eagle Football Group, propriétaire de l'Olympique Lyonnais se démarque dans le paysage français du sport professionnel.
Propriétaire de notre Stade, nous avons à cœur de respecter les enjeux socio-économiques tout en étant un acteur responsable et engagé dans la vie locale.

Notre dynamisme incarné par notre équipe masculine et notre Academy mixte nous incite à innover sans cesse et à nous adapter aux profonds changements de notre coeur de métier.

Nous recherchons un(e) Contrôleur de Gestion (H/F) en CDI à pourvoir dès à présent.

Véritable acteur du pilotage financier du Groupe, votre objectif sera de contribuer à la performance financière du Groupe en assurant le pilotage financier de l'entité OL Féminin, le contrôle de gestion des activités du Groupe, ainsi que la structuration des données, des outils et des processus du département Contrôle de Gestion.

Dans ce cadre, vos missions seront les suivantes :

- Pilotage financier de l'entité OL Féminin (prestation de services dédiée)

- Production et analyse des comptes de l'entité (P&L, bilan, masse salariale, trésorerie), en lien étroit avec la Direction Comptable ;
- Elaboration du budget de l'entité et des reportings budgétaires règlementaires (DNCG) selon le calendrier applicable ;
- Production du reporting à destination du management de l'entité et de l'actionnaire, en français et en anglais ;
- Interlocuteur privilégié des équipes opérationnelles et financières de l'entité dans le cadre du contrat de prestation, avec un suivi rigoureux du périmètre et des délais.

- Contrôle de gestion des activités du Groupe

- Contrôle budgétaire périodique des activités confiées et des directions du Groupe, et analyse des écarts (réel vs budget et n-1) ;
- Elaboration des comptes de résultat par activité et des analyses de marge à destination du Management ;
- Contribution aux cycles budgétaires du Groupe et aux analyses mensuelles de comptes consolidés et statutaires ;
- Participation aux clôtures mensuelles en collaboration étroite avec la Direction Comptable (provisions, rapprochements, contrôles de cohérence) ;
- Participation à la production des liasses règlementaires DNCG du club professionnel sur les sections confiées : liasses budgétaires (mai et octobre) et liasses réelles semestrielle et annuelle, en complément du reporting DNCG mensuel de l'entité OL Féminin.

- Données, analytique et amélioration des outils et processus

- Structuration et exploitation des données de gestion : requêtage, fiabilisation des bases, automatisation des travaux récurrents ;
- Maintien et développement des reportings existants ; participation active au projet data du Groupe, en lien avec les équipes IT et métiers ;
- Identification et déploiement d'usages d'intelligence artificielle appliqués au contrôle de gestion : automatisation des contrôles, détection d'anomalies, accélération des analyses d'écarts et de la production des reportings ;
- Pilotage de projets d'amélioration des processus et de développement de nouveaux outils de contrôle de gestion.

PROFIL :

De formation supérieure Bac +5 (Ecole de Commerce, Université, Master, etc.) avec une spécialisation en Finance d'Entreprise, Contrôle de Gestion, Comptabilité ou Audit, vous justifiez d'une expérience de 2 à 5 ans au sein d'un cabinet d'audit ou de conseil, ou d'une première expérience en contrôle de gestion, idéalement acquise dans un environnement multi-entités.

Nous recherchons les compétences techniques suivantes :

- Très bonne maîtrise de la comptabilité générale et analytique ;
- Maîtrise des règles comptables françaises ; la connaissance des normes IFRS est un plus,;
- Très bonne maîtrise des outils bureautiques de modélisation financière, notamment d'Excel ;
- Solide culture analytique et appétence marquée pour les usages de l'intelligence artificielle appliqués à la finance et au contrôle de gestion ;
- La pratique courante de l'anglais dans un cadre professionnel est un atout.

Nous apprécierons également vos qualités personnelles telles que votre rigueur, votre méthode et votre sens de l'organisation, ainsi que votre esprit critique, votre curiosité et votre sens relationnel développé, permettant de vous adapter à des environnements/métiers divers.

Tous les postes sont ouverts aux personnes en situation de handicap.

Pour vous donner un avant-goût de votre quotidien parmi nous, voici quelques-uns de nos avantages :

- Une vraie qualité de vie au travail, au cœur de notre politique RH (partenariat avec une salle de sport à proximité des bureaux, nombreux évènements conviviaux organisés tout au long de l’année, une assistance sociale à votre disposition) ;
- Un parcours d’intégration unique ;
- La possibilité de s’impliquer dans des actions sociales et solidaires.

Convaincu(e) ? N’hésitez plus, postulez !
